          %h2#idea Idea
          %h3#Generally Generally
          %p
            The
            %em product
            of two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributions"} distributions
            is an operation that generalizes, when defined, the ordinary pointwise product of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+functions"} generalized functions
            (via
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "non-singular+distribution#NonSingularDistributionsAreDenseInAllDistributions"} this prop.
          %p
            However, as opposed to ordinary functions, the product of distributions – if it is required to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension"} extend
            the pointwise product of functions and to satisfy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associativity"} associativity
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+law"} product law
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivatives+of+distributions"} derivatives of distributions
            – is not defined for arbitrary pairs of distributions, but only
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+function"} partially defined
            for those pairs whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform+of+distributions"} Fourier transforms
            satisfies a certain compatibility condition. Roughly: whenever the Fourier transform around any point of one factor does not decay exponentially in one direction of wave vectors, then the Fourier transform of the other factor has to decay exponentially in the
            %em opposite
            direction of wave vectors.
          %p
            This is known as
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H%C3%B6rmander%27s+criterion"} Hörmander's criterion
            on the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+front+set"} wave front set
            of the distributions (
            %a{:href => "#Hoermander90"}> Hörmander90
            ), and the study of distributions with attention to this condition is part of what is called
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/microlocal+analysis"} microlocal analysis
          %p
            (If one is willing to consider changing the
            %em ordinary
            pointwise product of functions, then is possible to define the product operation globally on all distributions, see at
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Colombeau+algebra"} Colombeau algebra
          %p
            The product of distributions with Hörmander’s condition on their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+front+set"} wave front set
            may be understood via
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform+of+distributions"} Fourier transform
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo ,
                  %mi v
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝒟
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u,v \in  \mathcal{D}'(\mathbb{R}^1)
            be two
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributions"} distributions
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
          %p
            Since the product
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \cdot v
            %em pointwise
            product of smooth functions, it must be fixed locally: for every point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \mathbb{R}
            there ought to be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+supported+function"} compactly supported
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bump+function"}> bump function
            )
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi C
                    %mi cp
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in C^\infty_{cp}(\mathbb{R})
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) = 1
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mi u
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi v
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  b^2 u \cdot v = (b u) \cdot (b v)
                  \\,.
          %p
            But now
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b v
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b u
            are both
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+supported+distributions"} compactly supported distributions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform+of+distributions"} Fourier transforms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi v
                    %mo ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{b v}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi u
                    %mo ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{b u}
            are, in particular,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
            (by the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paley-Wiener-Schwartz+theorem"} Paley-Wiener-Schwartz theorem
          %p
            Moreover, the operation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform"} Fourier transform
            intertwines pointwise products with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convolution+products"} convolution products
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \cdot v
            exists, it must locally be given by the inverse Fourier transform of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convolution+product"} convolution product
            of the Fourier transforms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi u
                    %mo ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat {b u}
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi b
                      %mo ^
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat b v
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi b
                        %mn 2
                      %mi u
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi v
                    %mo ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %munder
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mi max
                        %mo →
                        %mn ∞
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mi max
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mi max
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo −
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi d
                  %mi k
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\widehat{ b^2 u \cdot v }(x)
                  \\;=\;
                  \\underset{\underset{k_{max} \to \infty}{\longrightarrow}}{\lim}
                  \\,
                  \\int_{- k_{max}}^{k_{max}} \widehat{(b u)}(k) \widehat{(b v)}(x - k) d k
                  \\,.
          %p
            (Notice that the converse of this formula holds as a fact:
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "Fourier+transform#FourierTransformOfDistributionsInterchangesConvolutionOfDistributionsWithPointwiseProduct"} this prop.
          %p
            This shows that the product of distributions exists once there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bump+function"} bump function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            such that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral"} integral
            on the right converges as
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi max
                    %mo →
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_{max} \to \infty
          %p
            Now the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paley-Wiener-Schwartz+theorem"} Paley-Wiener-Schwartz theorem
            says more, it says that the Fourier transforms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi u
                    %mo ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat {b u}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi u
                    %mo ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat {b u}
            are polynomially bounded. On the other hand, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral"} integral
            above is well defined if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrand"} integrand
            decreases at least quadratically with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \to \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi u
                    %mo ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat {b u}
            has to polynomially decrease faster with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo →
                  %mo ±
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \to \pm \infty
            than
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi v
                    %mo ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat {b v}
            grows in the
            %em other
            direction,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo →
                  %mo ∓
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \to \mp \infty
            (due to the minus sign in the argument of the second factor in the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convolution+product"} convolution product
          %p
            Moreover, the degree of polynomial growth of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform+of+distributions"} Fourier transform
            increases by one with each
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivative+of+distributions"} derivative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+law"} product law
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivatives+of+distributions"} derivatives of distributions
            is to hold generally, we need that either
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi u
                    %mo ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{b u}
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mi v
                    %mo ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{b v}
            decays faster than
            %em any
            polynomial in the opposite of the directions in which the respective other factor does not decay.
          %p
            Here the set of directions of wave vectors in which the Fourier transform of a distribution localized around any point does not decay exponentially is called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+front+set"} wave front set
            of a distribution. Hence the condition that the product of two distributions is well defined is that for each wave vector direction in the wave front set of one of the two distributions, the opposite direction must not be an element of the wave front set of the other distribution.
          %h3#IdeaInPerturbativeQFT In perturbative quantum field theory
          %p
            The issue of mutliplying distributions has prominently been perceived in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator-valued+distributions"} operator-valued distributions
            serve to give the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+observables"} algebra of observables
            such as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+algebra"} Wick algebra
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+fields"} free fields
            or more generally the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interacting+field+algebra"} interacting field algebra
          %p
            A popular impression is (or has been) that the failure of distributions to have a globally defined product is a failure of the mathematical formalism to support the structures needed to model
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+front+set"} wave front set
            and handling the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point-extension+of+distributions"} point-extension of distributions
            properly via analysis of their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scaling+degree+of+a+distribution"} scaling degree
            leads to a mathematical rigorous construction and mathematically captures all the effects expected from the non-rigorous treatmeants, notably the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalization"} renormalization
            freedom. This is the topic of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+perturbation+theory"} causal perturbation theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+covariant+perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} locally covariant perturbative quantum field theory
          %h2#Definition Definition
          #ProductOfDistributions.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (multiplication of distributions)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ,
                    %mi v
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u,v \in \mathcal{D}'(X)
              be two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributions"} distributions
              such that the sum of their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+front+sets"} wave front sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi WF
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi WF
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} WF(u) + WF(v)
              does not intersect zero (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H%C3%B6rmander%27s+criterion"}> Hörmander's criterion
              ). Then their
              %em product distribution
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi v
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    u \cdot v \in \mathcal{D}'(X)
            %p
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+a+distribution"} pullback
              (via
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "pullback+of+a+distribution#PullbackOfDistributionsWhoseWaveFrontDoesNotIntersectNormalBundle"} this prop.
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+distributions"} tensor product
              along the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal"} diagonal
              map
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi X
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_X \;\colon\; X \to X \times X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi v
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    u \cdot v
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\Delta_X^\ast( u \otimes v )
                    \\,.
          #ProductOfDistributionsViaDiagonalPullbackOfTensorProductIsWellDefined.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductOfDistributions"}
              is indeed well defined.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hoermander90"}> Hörmander 90, theorem 8.2.10
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Melrose03"} Melrose 03, prop. 4.11
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              We need to check that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+distributions"} pullback of distributions
              is well defined. By
              %a{:href => "pullback+of+a+distribution#PullbackOfDistributionsWhoseWaveFrontDoesNotIntersectNormalBundle"} this prop.
              this means to check that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+front+set"} wave front set
              of the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \otimes v
              does not intersect the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conormal+bundle"} conormal bundle
              of the diagonal map
            %p Now the conormal bundle of the diagonal map consists of those pairs of covectors whose sum vanishes:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi N
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi X
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo ∈
                      %msubsup
                        %mi T
                        %mi x
                        %mo *
                      %mi X
                      %mo }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    N^\ast_{\Delta_X}
                    \=
                    \\left\{
                    (x,(\xi, -\xi))
                    \\;\vert\;
                    \\xi \in T^\ast_x X
                    \\right\}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Moreover, by
              %a{:href => "tensor+product+of+distributions#WaveFrontOfTensorProductDistribution"} this example
              the wave front set of the tensor product distribution
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \otimes v
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi WF
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi WF
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi WF
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∪
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi supp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi u
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ×
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi WF
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∪
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi WF
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi supp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ×
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    WF(u \otimes v)
                    \\;\subset\;
                    \\left(
                    WF(u) \times WF(v)
                    \\right)
                    \\;\cup\;
                    \\left(
                    \\left( supp(u) \times \{0\} \right)
                    \\times WF(v)
                    \\right)
                    \\;\cup\;
                    \\left(
                    WF(u)
                    \\times
                    \\left(
                    supp(v) \times \{0\}
                    \\right)
                    \\right)
                    \\,,
            %p
              Since any wave front set excludes the zero-section by definition, the second and the third summand in this union never intersect the above conormal bundle. The first summand intersects the above conormal bundle precisely if there is a covector in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi WF
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} WF(u)
              which is minus a covector contained in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi WF
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} WF(v)
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#general General
          #WaveFrontSetOfProductOfDistributionsInsideFiberProductOfFactorWaveFrontSets.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+front+set"} wave front set
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+of+distributions"} product of distributions
                is inside
                = succeed "-wise" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sum"} sum
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+front+sets"} wave front sets
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ,
                    %mi v
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u,v \in \mathcal{D}'(X)
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributions"} distributions
              satisfying
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H%C3%B6rmander%27s+criterion"} Hörmander's criterion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \cdot v
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductOfDistributions"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductOfDistributionsViaDiagonalPullbackOfTensorProductIsWellDefined"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+front+set"} wave front set
              of the product distribution is contained inside the fiberwise
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sum"} sum
              of the wave front set elements of the two factors:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi WF
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi WF
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi WF
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    WF(u \cdot v)
                    \\;\subset\;
                    (WF(u) \cup (X \times \{0\}))
                    +
                    (WF(v) \cup (X \times \{0\}))
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hoermander90"}> Hörmander 90, theorem 8.2.10
            )
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              By def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductOfDistributions"}
              and prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductOfDistributionsViaDiagonalPullbackOfTensorProductIsWellDefined"}
              we have
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi v
                      %mo =
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi X
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi u
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \cdot v = \Delta_X^\ast(u \otimes v)
              %a{:href => "tensor+product+of+distributions#WaveFrontOfTensorProductDistribution"} this example
              the wave front set of the tensor product distribution
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u \otimes v
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi WF
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi WF
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi WF
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∪
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi supp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi u
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ×
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi WF
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∪
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi WF
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi supp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ×
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    WF(u \otimes v)
                    \\;\subset\;
                    \\left(
                    WF(u) \times WF(v)
                    \\right)
                    \\;\cup\;
                    \\left(
                    \\left( supp(u) \times \{0\} \right)
                    \\times WF(v)
                    \\right)
                    \\;\cup\;
                    \\left(
                    WF(u)
                    \\times
                    \\left(
                    supp(v) \times \{0\}
                    \\right)
                    \\right)
            %p
              and by
              %a{:href => "pullback+of+a+distribution#PullbackOfDistributionsWhoseWaveFrontDoesNotIntersectNormalBundle"} this prop.
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi WF
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi X
                      %mo *
                    %mi WF
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi u
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi WF
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi u
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    WF(\Delta_X^\ast (u \otimes v))
                    \\subset
                    \\Delta_X^\ast WF(u \otimes v)
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\left\{
                    (x, k_1 + k_2 )
                    \\;\vert\;
                    ((x,k_1),(x,k_2))
                    \\in
                    WF(u \otimes v)
                    \\right\}
                    \\,.
          %p More generally:
          #PartialProductOfDistributionsOfSeveralVariables.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (partial product of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributions+of+several+variables"} distributions of several variables
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAA
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    K_1 \in \mathcal{D}'(X \times Y)
                    \\phantom{AAA}
                    K_2 \in \mathcal{D}'(Y \times Z)
            %p
              be two
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributions+of+two+variables"} distributions of two variables
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+of+distributions"} product of distributions
              to be defined over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H%C3%B6rmander%27s+criterion"} Hörmander's criterion
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+front+sets"} wave front sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi WF
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi WF
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} WF(K_1), WF(K_2)
              needs to hold for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+front+set"} wave front
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+vectors"} wave vectors
              along
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              taken to be zero.
            %p
              If this is satisfied, then composition of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+kernels"} integral kernels
              (if it exists)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi Y
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi dvol
                      %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (K_1 \circ K_2)(-,-)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\underset{Y}{\int}
                    K_1(-,y) K_2(y,-)
                    dvol_Y(y)
                    \\;\in\;
                    \\mathcal{D}'(X \times Z)
            %p
              has
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+front+set"} wave front set
              constrained by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi WF
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi WF
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi WF
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∪
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi WF
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Z
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∪
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi WF
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    WF'(K_1 \circ K_2)
                    \\;\subset\;
                    WF'(K_1) \circ WF'(K_2)
                    \\;\cup\;
                    (X \times \{0\}) \times WF'(K_2)_Z
                    \\;\cup\;
                    WF(K_1)_X \times (Z \times \{0\})
                    \\,,
            %p
              where on the left the composition symbol means composition of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relations"} relations
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+vectors"} wave vectors
              over points in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            #eq:CompositionOfIntegralKernelsWaveFronConstraint.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi WF
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi z
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi x
                                %mo ,
                                %mi y
                                %mo ,
                                %msub
                                  %mi k
                                  %mi x
                                %mo ,
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %msub
                                  %mi k
                                  %mi y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi WF
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi K
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %mtext and
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi y
                                %mo ,
                                %mi z
                                %mo ,
                                %msub
                                  %mi k
                                  %mi y
                                %mo ,
                                %msub
                                  %mi k
                                  %mi z
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi WF
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi K
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mtext or
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %msub
                                  %mi k
                                  %mi x
                                %mo =
                                %mn 0
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %mtext and
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi y
                                %mo ,
                                %mi z
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 0
                                %mo ,
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %msub
                                  %mi k
                                  %mi z
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi WF
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi K
                                  %mn 2
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mtext or
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %msub
                                  %mi k
                                  %mi z
                                %mo =
                                %mn 0
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %mtext and
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi x
                                %mo ,
                                %mi y
                                %mo ,
                                %msub
                                  %mi k
                                  %mi x
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 0
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi WF
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi K
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo )
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    WF(K_1 \circ K_2)
                    \\;\subset\;
                    \\left\{
                    (x,z, k_x, k_z)
                    \\;\vert\;
                    \\array{
                    \\left(
                    (x,y,k_x,-k_y) \in WF(K_1)
