          %h3#NonExistenceOfAGlobalProduct Non-existence of a global product
          %p
            The fact that there is no general extension of multiplication to distributions (without condition on the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+front+set"} wave front set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/no-go+theorem"} no-go theorem
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laurent+Schwartz"} Laurent Schwartz
          %p A quick way to see the problem is the following:
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(x)
            be the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heaviside+function"} Heaviside function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H(x) = H^{n} (x)
          %p where the product on the right side is the product of classical functions. Applying differentiation and the product rule naivly results in a contradiction immediatly:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi n
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\delta(x) = n H^{n-1} (x) \delta(x)
          %p
            The inconsistency of this product is detected by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+front+sets"} wave front sets
            as follows: The wave front set both of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heaviside+distribution"} Heaviside distribution
            as well as of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delta+distribution"} delta distribution
            on the line is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi k
                  %mo ≠
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{(0,k) \vert k \neq 0\}
            (
            %a{:href => "wavefront+set#WaveFrontOfDeltaDistribution"} this example
            and
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "wavefront+set#WaveFrontSetOfHeavisideDistribution"} this example
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductOfDistributions"}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            for which there exists a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bump+function"} bump function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b(0) = 1
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \cdot u
            is again a bump function. This excludes the products of these distributions with themselves and with each other.
          %h2#Examples Examples
          #ProductOfADistributionWithANonSingularDistribution.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (product of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distribution"} distribution
                with a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-singular+distributions"} non-singular distributions
                is
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+of+a+distribution+with+a+smooth+function"} product of a distribution with a smooth function
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wave+front+set"} wave front set
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-singular+distribution"} non-singular distribution
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_f
              corresponding to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty"} empty
              (
              %a{:href => "Paley-Wiener-Schwartz+theorem#DecayPropertyOfFourierTransformOfCompactlySupportedFunctions"}> this prop.
              ). Therefore the product of distributions (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductOfDistributions"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-singular+distribution"} non-singular distribution
              with any distribution
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
              is defined, and given by the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+of+distributions+with+smooth+functions"} product of distributions with smooth functions
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mi f
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi u
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi u
                    %mo =
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    u_f \cdot u = f \cdot u = u(f\cdot (-))
                    \\,.
